From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 07:33:46 -0500
Subject: feat: a stalled update download tries again, and About says how to
 retry

An update download that fails, or gets no byte for a minute, starts over
ten seconds later, three tries in all, before the failure is said (updates
Up25; BACKLOG S-420). The owner's Mac updated from beta 9 with GitHub's
connection gone quiet at 38%: CFNetwork gave up after a minute, Sparkle
called the update failed, and nothing said a reload would try again.

On the Mac a try is a new check, because Sparkle downloads only in a session
of its own: its delegate says the download failed, the session ends, and
didFinishUpdateCycleForUpdateCheck, its last word, starts the ten seconds. A
download the user watches goes on saying Updating; one on the schedule tries
again as quietly as it failed. A yes given to a version covers all its tries
(Up4). A failure after the download arrived is not tried again.

On Windows the updater now has its own stall timer. The request's two-hour
timeout was all there was, so a connection that went quiet held the download
and the page's percentage until it ran out.

A failure on the About page now says how to try again (Up5): reload the
page with automatic updates on, because it checks when it opens; off, the
Check for Updates command. A failed download and an unreachable feed say
Stedding's own sentences on the Mac too, because Sparkle's end in "Please
try again later", which that advice would contradict.

Why: the owner's update stopped at 38% and ended in an error that gave no
way forward, and a connection that goes quiet is not the user's to notice.

Removable when: never as behaviour; the Mac's half goes when Sparkle retries
a failed download itself.
